6-11-25T15:00:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50571004/2026-college-football-week-13-top-25-betting-lines-odds","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Manuel to remain Michigan AD until new hire is found","description":"Warde Manuel has agreed to stay in the job as Michigan's athletic director until the school finds a new athletic director, sources told ESPN on Wednesday.","published":"2026-11-25T16:12:47.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50592920/sources-manuel-stay-job-new-michigan-ad-hired","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel and Dan Wetzel","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Bottom 10 after Week 12: How the Bruins put the 'L' in UCLA","description":"While UCLA suffered its first loss, we still have a team looking for its first win -- and time is running out.","published":"2026-11-25T12:14:25.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50585901/bottom-10-week-12-ucla","type":"Story","byline":"Ryan McGee","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5145410/chris-cole","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Cole_(linebacker)"},"pick":{"pick":9,"round":1,"team":"PHI","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Chris Cole (linebacker)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Cole_(linebacker)","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-22T23:50:20Z","intro":"Christopher Cole (born October 3, 2005) is an American college football linebacker for the Georgia Bulldogs.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Cole attended Salem High School in Salem, Virginia. As a junior, he recorded 76 tackles and 11 tackles-for-loss. A four-star recruit and one of the top-rated players in the state of Virginia, Cole committed to play college football at the University of Georgia over offers from Miami, Penn State, and Tennessee."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a true freshman, Cole totaled 16 tackles and two fumble recoveries, being named to the SEC All-Freshman Team. Entering the 2025 season, he was expected to earn a bigger role in the Bulldogs defense. Cole finished the season recording 60 tackles and 4.5 sacks.Against Oklahoma in 2026, he recorded a sack and two fumble recoveries, returning one 85 yards for a touchdown in a 41–13 victory. Cole was named SEC Defensive Player of the Week for his performance. He was named a Butkus Award semifinalist in October."}]}}